{%- comment -%}
  The sidebar navigation rail, rendered from _data/navigation.yml groups
  (publications / schulungen / about) via _includes/sidebar.html.

  2026-08-05 — the collapse mechanism was rebuilt. It used to be the theme's
  CSS-checkbox accordion:

      <input id="ac-toc" type="checkbox" />
      <label for="ac-toc">Menü ein-/ausschalten</label>

  which was inaccessible in two separate ways below $large (1024px):

    1. _navigation.scss hides `input[type="checkbox"], label` at every width and
       re-shows only the LABEL on small screens. The <input> stayed
       `display: none` — so it was not focusable — and a <label> is not
       focusable either. There was no keyboard path to open the rail at all,
       on the 17 pages where this rail IS the site's structure.

    2. The collapsed panel used `max-height: 0; opacity: 0; overflow: hidden`,
       which does NOT remove children from the tab order. A keyboard user
       tabbing past the toggle landed on 5-8 links they could not see.

  Now: a real <button aria-expanded aria-controls>, and the panel collapses with
  `display: none` (see assets/css/arc42-de.css) so hidden links leave the tab
  order. Behaviour lives in assets/js/arc42-nav.js.

  Progressive enhancement: the button is hidden and the panel is always open
  unless <html> carries the `js` class (set in _includes/head.html). With
  JavaScript off, the rail renders expanded — long, but never unreachable.

  The panel id is derived from the nav group name so a page including two rails
  cannot emit duplicate ids.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% assign navigation = site.data.navigation[include.nav] %}
{% assign panel_id = 'nav-items-' | append: include.nav %}

<nav class="nav__list" aria-label="{{ site.data.ui-text[site.locale].menu_label | default: 'Toggle Menu' }}">
  {% if page.sidebar.title %}<h3 class="nav__title" style="padding-left: 0;">{{ page.sidebar.title }}</h3>{% endif %}
  <button class="nav__toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="{{ panel_id }}">
    {{ site.data.ui-text[site.locale].menu_label | default: "Toggle Menu" }}
  </button>
  <ul class="nav__items" id="{{ panel_id }}">
    {% for nav in navigation %}
      <li>
        {% if nav.url %}
          <a href="{{ nav.url | relative_url }}"{% if nav.url == page.url %} class="active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}><span class="nav__sub-title">{{ nav.title }}</span></a>
        {% else %}
          <span class="nav__sub-title">{{ nav.title }}</span>
        {% endif %}

        {% if nav.children != null %}
        <ul>
          {% for child in nav.children %}
            <li><a href="{{ child.url | relative_url }}"{% if child.url == page.url %} class="active" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ child.title }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</nav>
